            0.12
          ],
          "content": "179"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.163,
            0.896,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "| Percentage of female teachers | Number of states/U.T.(f<sub>i</sub>) | x<sub>i</sub> | d<sub>i</sub> = x<sub>i</sub>- 50 | <sub>ui</sub> =xi -5010 | f<sub>i</sub>x<sub>i</sub> | f<sub>i</sub>d<sub>i</sub> | f<sub>i</sub>u<sub>i</sub> |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 15 - 2525 - 3535 - 4545 - 5555 - 6565 - 7575 - 85 | 61174421 | 20304050607080 | -30-20-100102030 | -3-2-10123 | 12033028020024014080 | -180-220-700404030 | -18-22-70443 |\n| Total | 35 |  |  |  | 1390 | -360 | -36 |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.441,
                0.138,
                0.558,
                0.157
              ],
              "content": "Table 13.7"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.147,
                0.456,
                0.695,
                0.479
              ],
              "content": "From the table above, we obtain $\\Sigma f_{i} = 35$ , $\\Sigma f_{i}x_{i} = 1390,$"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.395,
            0.484,
            0.678,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": "\\Sigma f_{i}d_{i}=-360,\\quad \\Sigma f_{i}u_{i}=-36.",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.52,
            0.642,
            0.566
          ],
          "content": "Using the direct method, $\\bar{x}=\\frac{\\Sigma f_{i}x_{i}}{\\Sigma f_{i}}=\\frac{1390}{35}=39.71$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.567,
            0.475,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": "Using the assumed mean method,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.322,
            0.6,
            0.702,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "\\overline{x}=a+\\frac{\\Sigma f_{i}d_{i}}{\\Sigma f_{i}}=50+\\frac{(-360)}{35}=39.71",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.649,
            0.465,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": "Using the step-deviation method,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.32,
            0.681,
            0.818,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": "\\bar{x}=a+\\left(\\frac{\\Sigma f_{i}u_{i}}{\\Sigma f_{i}}\\right)\\times h=50+\\left(\\frac{-36}{35}\\right)\\times10=39.71",
          "image_source": "images/page_8_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.737,
            0.902,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the mean percentage of female teachers in the primary schools of rural areas is 39.71."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.78,
            0.903,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": "**Remark :** The result obtained by all the three methods is the same. So the choice of method to be used depends on the numerical values of $x _ { i }$ and $f _ { i ^ { * } }$ If $x _ { i }$ and $f _ { i }$ are sufficiently small, then the direct method is an appropriate choice. If $x _ { i }$ and $f _ { i }$ are numerically large numbers, then we can go for the assumed mean method or step-deviation method. If the class sizes are unequal, and $x _ { i }$ are large numerically, we can still apply the step-deviation method by taking h to be a suitable divisor of all the $d _ { i } ^ { \\flat }$ s."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
